        "senderName": "NWS Corpus Christi TX",
        "headline": "Wind Advisory issued October 16 at 6:41PM CDT until October 17 at 1:00AM CDT by NWS Corpus Christi TX",
        "description": "* WHAT...North winds 20 to 30 mph with gusts up to 40 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Bee, Coastal Aransas, Coastal Calhoun, Coastal Kleberg,\nCoastal Nueces, Coastal Refugio, Coastal San Patricio, Goliad,\nInland Calhoun, Inland Kleberg, Inland Nueces, Inland Refugio,\nInland San Patricio, Jim Wells, and Victoria Counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 1 AM CDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree\nlimbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.",
        "instruction": "Winds this strong can make driving difficult, especially for high\nprofile vehicles. Use extra caution.",
