        "headline": "Flood Advisory issued October 16 at 2:05PM CDT until October 17 at 7:00AM CDT by NWS Norman OK",
        "description": "...The National Weather Service in Norman has issued a Flood Advisory\nfor the following rivers in Texas...\n\nBrazos River at Seymour affecting Knox and Baylor Counties.\n\n* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Brazos River at Seymour.\n\n* WHEN...From this afternoon to Saturday morning.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 10.0 feet, The river remains within its banks in\nsouthern Knox and southern Baylor counties.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1:45 PM CDT Friday the stage was 10.0 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 12.0 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to rise to a crest of 10.1 feet\nthis evening.\n- Action stage is 10.0 feet.\n- Flood stage is 12.0 feet.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
        "instruction": "If you encounter a flooded roadway, turn around and find an\nalternative route.\n\nAdditional information is available at www.weather.gov.\n\nThe next statement will be issued late tonight at 215 AM CDT.",
        "response": "Avoid",
